CANONICAL EO OPTION B. This is the joint TermAl and Engram wording, identical to Engram memory rules-greg-native-clean-before-b-2026-11-06 and rules-source-identity-2026-11-03. It was recorded by Termal::Fable2 at 2026-11-06 16:28Z, per Greg via Asistant: „EO nie mialo tego uzywac, mialo sprawdzac tylko stan przed i PO wariant B ABY ... TO UPROSCIC” and „prosze o sprawdzenie memory, dokumentow ZAPISANIE POPRAWNEGO WARIANTU”. Rev 3 adds Greg's clarification (#576): NO hashing of the .git directory at all; the earlier wording limited to .git/info was wrong. It supersedes every earlier option-B text, including the 05:52Z point (4) "the file watcher can only DISQUALIFY", and all watcher, H3, .git/info and source-v2 decisions of 2026-11-06.
EO OPTION B credit requires ONLY:
(a) a clean source_id at commit X, taken before the turn's prompt is dispatched;
(b) the declared test is the turn's first tool action;
(c) a clean source_id at the same X after the test;
(d) the result recorded with the existing verification_record_v1 (plus the existing artifact, identity and claim checks).
NO watcher condition of any kind, NO hashing or comparing of anything in the .git directory, no submodule scope list, no other gate.
source_id = `engram source` v1, the only version: root HEAD, the filter guard, submodule status --recursive with all rows ' ', one root git status with --ignore-submodules=none, HEAD reread. No ls-files.
ACCEPTED LIMITS: a change reverted before the after-test capture; anything git status doesn't report (hidden index flags, .git/info edits); ignored files.
Rule: no new conditions, mechanisms or gates on this model without Greg's explicit word. Work items: w-24a72c898d6d and w-6f42c416b0c7 (v1 only). Central work is PAUSED by Greg since 16:25Z.
